# std — standard library
File: website/pulled/std.oot

Source: openOODA/std/docs/

## What it is

The library you import. Tag v1.0.8. Eight functional domains.
Each domain has its own `ANCHOR.oo`. Counted on 2026-09-04:
188 `ANCHOR.oo` front doors, 5813 `.oo` files. Do not use the
old "173 modules" figure.

Zero ambient authority. Effects take an explicit cap token.
The install script clones std with the toolchain.

## Surface

| Domain | Scope |
|--------|-------|
| `core` | Option, Result, List, math, text, encoding |
| `fs` | Files, OS, time, archive under Fs caps |
| `net` | HTTP, TCP, UDP, sync, actor under Net caps |
| `sec` | Hash, AEAD, capability, RASP, constant-time |
| `science` | Physics, chem, bio, econ |
| `app` | AI tensors, UI, agents, data |
| `hw` | Architecture theory (x86, RISC-V, GPU) |
| `meta` | Test harnesses and diagnostics |

Import a domain through its `ANCHOR.oo`. Do not add files
under `std/` unless the user asks for library expansion
(RULES.oot §1.22).
